  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.10\n- Feature scope is one need's delivery: a component shared by two features no longer merges them in review-feature or the feature document.\n- Evidence must lie beneath .octoevidence-evidence/ (path traversal refused); doctor re-hashes every claimed artifact; reconcile reports tampering.\n- task.* properties are written only by the change workflow; planned -> approved needs a human; a closed change can be re-cited and accepted again.\n- Four eyes: whoever proposed or revised a record does not accept it. Repeated decisions and rejecting a depended-on record are refused.\n- Feature documents cite their observations and trace, use one lifecycle derived from the need, and stop being current when a record joins the feature.\n- The brief finds the need through any relation, names the existing change, and a story or key is created once.\n- Roles trimmed to the four-role team plus coordinator; modes are delivery and knowledge; MCP refusals carry their reason; records store non-ASCII text as written.\n- New: `octoevidence serve`, a loopback web portal where each role sees what waits on its decision, proposes and revises knowledge, and records decisions under its own name.",
